    <fr:title text="Fiber of a Map">Fiber of a Map</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f:A\to  B]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y:B]]></fr:tex>. The <html:strong>fiber of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y]]></fr:tex></html:strong> is the
    type of elements of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> equipped with an identification of their image
    with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y]]></fr:tex>:
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \mathsf {fib}_f(y)
        :\equiv 
        \Sigma _{x:A}\bigl (f(x)=y\bigr ).
    ]]></fr:tex>
    Thus a term of the fiber is a pair <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(x,p)]]></fr:tex> with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x:A]]></fr:tex> and
    <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p:f(x)=y]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
